    <!-- THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE <Layout>
         breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent
         xml file" error.

         BUSINESS FIELDS ADDED 2026-08-20 (UAT gap). Until now this layout was a STUB: it carried
         exactly four fields, Name, OwnerId, CreatedById and LastModifiedById, and not one business
         field. This is the third of the three disposition child layouts found empty in the same UAT
         pass, alongside BOV_Submission__c and Disposition_Offer__c.

         WHY IT SURVIVED TO UAT: every read path bypasses layouts. BrokerListingSelector names its
         columns in SOQL and lwc/brokerListing renders them itself, so the listing card looked
         complete while the create and detail screens were empty.

         🔴 THE SYMPTOM DIFFERS FROM ITS TWO SIBLINGS, AND THAT IS WORTH KNOWING BEFORE ANYONE
         RETESTS. Nothing navigates to a standard "new Broker Listing" modal: lwc/brokerListing has
         no NavigationMixin create call, and the record is created in Apex by
         DispositionStageEntryService, which stamps Listing_Status__c to its initial value. So the
         empty layout was never blocking a CREATE here the way "+ Log Offer" was; it was blanking
         the DETAIL and EDIT screens of a record the service had already made. Disposition__c is
         placed below anyway, because a lookup absent from the layout is invisible on the detail
         page and cannot be repaired by hand if the service ever links the wrong parent.

         BEHAVIOUR RULES APPLIED:
         1. NO FORMULA FIELDS EXIST ON THIS OBJECT. All nine custom fields were checked in
            objects/Broker_Listing__c/fields/; none carries a formula element.
         2. 🔴 PARTIALLY SUPERSEDED 2026-08-21 (offer-form-and-stage-retirement.md, Request B).
            RETRACTED, quoted rather than deleted because it is the reasoning a future reader
            would otherwise rebuild from: "NO MACHINE OWNED FIELD EXISTS ON THIS OBJECT EITHER,
            so every business field below is Edit." That is no longer true of
            Call_For_Offers_Date__c specifically - see its own note below. Every OTHER business
            field on this object is still Edit for the reasoning originally given here: the only
            Apex write to any field on this object is DispositionStageEntryService setting
            Listing_Status__c at creation, and a one time initial value is not the same thing as
            an automation that owns a field for its lifetime. Days_On_Market__c and
            Offers_Received__c in particular LOOK derived and are NOT: no Apex, trigger or Flow
            writes either one, and both are only ever read, so locking them would leave them
            permanently at their default. Offers_Received__c is a plain Number with defaultValue
            0, not a roll up summary.
         3. Name stays Readonly. It is an AutoNumber, displayFormat BL-{0000}.

         🔴 Call_For_Offers_Date__c -> Readonly, 2026-08-21 (Request B). NOT YET MACHINE-OWNED -
         no Apex, trigger or Flow writes it today, so rule 2 above does not literally apply - but
         it is RESERVED for a future automation the user has explicitly deferred ("will create
         its proper flow later on"). The field itself has no required=true, no validation rule
         (this object has none at all), and no reader that breaks on null, so a blank value was
         always safe; the smallest honest change is this one word, not a validation rule or a
         stamp. FLS in DPEG_Disposition_Edit is DELIBERATELY LEFT editable=true - flipping it
         would be a large-blast-radius PermissionSet edit (a PermissionSet deploy replaces its
         whole fieldPermissions set) for one word of intent, and the deferred automation will
         need that grant back regardless. Layout behaviour alone expresses "not hand-entered"
         precisely and reversibly. Seed data already populates this field four times over
         (scripts/seed-disposition*.apex, TestDataFactory.createBrokerListing) with no change
         needed here.

         THIS OBJECT HAS NO APPROVAL PROCESS, so unlike its two siblings it correctly has no
         relatedLists block and no RelatedProcessHistoryList. Nothing was removed. -->
